{# How many rows this section holds, what they add up to, and how much of the file was read to find
   them.

   The count is counted in PHP from rows already fetched, never with a COUNT query: this screen caps
   its feeds and counts neither with SQL, and AdminListScreenConventionsCest reads "one request ran
   both a counting and a limiting query rooted at table X" as "this screen is X's list screen".
   A count(*) here would make this worklist claim to be the purchase order list AND the vendor bill
   list. It is a worklist; it has no pager.

   The total is shown only when every row in the section is in one currency. A purchase document
   carries its own currency and this application never converts one — see
   AbstractPurchaseDocument::$currency — so adding CAD to USD would produce the most confident wrong
   number on the page.

   ## The cap says so now

   `scan` is what the feed READ: how many documents its query matched, and how many of them the cap
   let it look at. They are documents, not rows — one bill can raise several exception lines — so
   this is a second sentence rather than a bigger number inside the first. Without it, a file of 205
   exception-carrying bills rendered 200 rows under "Showing 1 to 200 of 200 bill exceptions", which
   reads as the whole of it and is how bill 201 went missing with nothing on screen to suggest it
   had. Rendered only when the cap actually bit: a worklist that reports its own internals on every
   page view is noise, and noise is what a person stops reading. #}
<div class="table-footer">
    {% include 'admin/_table_count.html.twig' with {count: count, total: count, label: label} only %}
    {% if total is not null %}
        <span class="table-count">{{ total.currency }} {{ total.amount }} at risk</span>
    {% elseif count > 0 %}
        <span class="table-count">Not totalled: these rows are in more than one currency, and purchase documents are never converted.</span>
    {% endif %}
    {% if scan is defined and scan.available > scan.scanned %}
        <span class="table-count" id="{{ scanId }}">
            Read from the most recent {{ scan.scanned }} of {{ scan.available }} {{ scanLabel }};
            {{ scan.available - scan.scanned }} not examined. Narrow the filter to reach the rest.
        </span>
    {% endif %}
</div>
